 Unlike standard 3D voxel grids, Grid-NeRF factorizes the 3D feature grid into:
-1.  **2D Ground Feature Planes:** A set of feature planes spanning the $xy$-plane (ground level) [S1].
-2.  **Vertical Shared Vector:** A feature vector shared along the $z$-axis [S1].
