 ## Subtopics
 
 ### HashNeRF
-Uses hierarchical hash tables for multi-resolution encoding without explicit grid factorization [G]. Choose when memory efficiency is critical and scene is not strictly urban/ground-dominant [8678-hashnerf.md].
+Uses hierarchical hash tables for multi-resolution encoding without explicit grid factorization [G]. Choose when memory efficiency is critical and scene is not strictly urban/ground-dominant [G].
 
 ### Surface-Relative Hash Encoding
-Encodes features relative to a surface mesh rather than absolute coordinates [G]. Choose when explicit geometry is available and surface detail is paramount [18178-surface-relative-hash-encoding.md].
+Encodes features relative to a surface mesh rather than absolute coordinates [G]. Choose when explicit geometry is available and surface detail is paramount [G].
 
 ### HyRF (Hybrid Radiance Fields)
-Combines explicit and implicit representations to balance rendering speed and geometric accuracy [G]. Choose when hybrid scene modeling is required [19187-hyrf-hybrid-radiance-fields.md].
+Combines explicit and implicit representations to balance rendering speed and geometric accuracy [G]. Choose when hybrid scene modeling is required [G].
 
 ### Neural Pre-integrated Emitters (NEF)
-Models volumetric light transport using neural pre-integrated emitters [G]. Choose when simulating participating media or volumetric lighting is required [19201-neural-pre-integrated-emitters-nef.md].
+Models volumetric light transport using neural pre-integrated emitters [G]. Choose when simulating participating media or volumetric lighting is required [G].
 
